  "source": "home_assistant",
  "row": "solarman",
  "vendor": "deye",
  "cardNeedsValues": true,
  "note": "DEYE-022 (docs/28-deye-inverter-control.md sections 3 and 5.2): a Deye hybrid through ha-solarman (davidrapan/ha-solarman ac1d88b, deye_p3.yaml and deye_hybrid.yaml), read only. entity: <domain>.<ha-solarman key> (the unique_id <entry id>_<key>_<platform> without entry id and platform; one name for both definitions); values: option -> catalog code. unverified until DEYE-001 (the tester snapshot). row: the Home Assistant inverter row (HomeAssistantInverterProfile id) whose posts carry these settings (DEYE-013: the component posts them under the integration solarman_deye); vendor deye turns the Settings card (PAR-010) on once this source stored a value for the plant (cardNeedsValues, DEYE-030 P2: no empty card before component 0.30.0 posts them, none on a Deye Cloud plant). readbackData: the read service fields, {device} the inverter HA device id and {address} the register (ha-solarman ac1d88b services.py: device, address 0-65535, count 0-125, answer {address: u16}); uniqueId: the unique id of a setting entity ({entry} the ha-solarman entry id, {platform} the entity domain). settingsControl is the write binding of the family file, for unit 4: per definition the register of every role (address, scale per LP3/HP3 variant, range in catalog units, raw: register value -> catalog code, rawBit0: the code of any other value with bit 0 set, encoding hhmm: HH*100+MM), definitions: how the Device register picks the definition and variant (the variant is max(detected, the entry option)), neverTouched: addresses no binding may name, readback: the fresh read service, clock and backupLoad: read only. Nothing is written by this unit.",
